# Where this machine keeps things. Copy to `.env` and edit; `.env` is not
# committed, because a path on one machine is not a fact about the project.
#
# Read by package.sh before it settles anything, and only into names nothing has
# already set — so a one-off `WITCHLIGHT_SERVICE_REPO=... ./package.sh` still
# wins over what is written here.

# The map service's repository. package.sh builds it from here with
# `cargo build --release` and bundles the binary into the server archive, and it
# is where THIRD-PARTY.md is read from. Required for a server archive, unless a
# built binary is named outright with --service.
WITCHLIGHT_SERVICE_REPO=/path/to/rust/witchlight

# A built map service binary, used instead of building one. Only for a machine
# that cannot build the service at all; naming this skips the cargo build.
#WITCHLIGHT_SERVICE=/path/to/witchlight

# The third-party notice for that binary, if it is not in the repository above.
#WITCHLIGHT_NOTICES=/path/to/THIRD-PARTY.md
